            "review_title": "Review at Manwah - Taiwanese Hot Pot Saigon Centre",
            "review_text": "hoanghac13\nSan Jose, California641 contributions\n0\nStill my go to hotpot spot whenever I’m in town\nJul 2026 • Family\nI actually prefer the mala broth here at Man Wah over Dao Niu Guo — the flavor just hits differently and I keep coming back for it.\n\nOn the beef, I’m Team Frozen for mala/spicy pot specifically. The frozen slices are paper-thin and soft, which cuts right through the ligaments and fiber — perfect texture for a spicy broth. Hand-cut is fresher, sure, but if it’s not sliced thin enough it can turn tough and chewy, which might be why it sometimes comes out crumpled into small pieces, almost like bò băm. My take: hand-cut works better in a clear broth pot, where you can actually appreciate that freshness without the toughness getting in the way.\nRead more\nWritten July 21, 2026",
